 ## 3. Equality budgets, primitivity and rank-one exclusion
 
-A cyclic word x is K-unique when its m cyclic length-K substrings have different starting positions. If two distinct starts have equal K-substrings, their K equality edges form a graph of maximum degree2, with no loops or repeated unordered edges when K<=m/4. Its paths and simple cycles impose equality rank at least K/2. Reveal the four open chains sequentially: at most four forced visits can occur at chain starts; each remaining forced transition costs q. Together with q^4 connectors, the fixed-length exceptional weight is at most N^4 q^(K/2) for K>=8. Fewer than m² substring-start pairs, O(m³) length quadruples, m² roots and the N^-2 band normalization give O_w(N^10 q^(K/2)). This is an absolute bound only on the exceptional set, not the complete spectral sum.
